I implemented the second plan task: a new file, `src/game.js`, holds the Tetris game rules with no terminal input or output. Nothing uses it yet. Hooking it up to keys and the screen is the next task, so `npm start` still only shows a title and waits for `q`. I didn't write any test files. I checked it with a quick throwaway script: dropping pieces filled the board and ended the game, a single-line clear cleared the row and scored 100, and rotating and moving worked.

- **Board and pieces:** a 10Ã20 board with all seven tetrominoes, which come in shuffled sets of seven.
- **Movement and rotation:** pieces move left and right, and rotate either way using the standard wall-kick rules.
- **Dropping:** gravity moves the piece down one row per step. A soft drop scores 1 point per row and a hard drop scores 2. There is also a landing-position preview (the "ghost").
- **Lines and levels:** full lines are cleared and score 100, 300, 500 or 800 for one to four lines, times the level. The level goes up every 10 lines, and pieces fall faster at each level.
- **Spawning and game over:** a "next piece" is kept for preview. The game ends when a new piece has no room to appear, and it can be paused and reset.

